#!/bin/bash
# bande-desktop alone, without recommends, brings a login window and sound and no X server; the
# Bande login window is the display manager through its own PAM service, whose pictures folder only
# it reads, and purging it hands the display to greetd.
set -euo pipefail
for package in bande-greeter greetd pipewire wireplumber; do
    [ "$(dpkg-query -W -f '${db:Status-Status}' "$package")" = installed ] || { echo "$package is missing"; exit 1; }
done

x11=$(dpkg-query -W -f '${db:Status-Status} ${Package}\n' | awk '$1 == "installed" { print $2 }' |
    grep -E '^(xserver-|xwayland$|xorg$|x11-session-utils$|xinit$)' || true)
[ -z "$x11" ] || { echo "installed: $x11"; exit 1; }

greetd_config=/usr/share/bande-greeter/greetd-config.toml
grep -qx "ExecStart=/usr/sbin/greetd --config $greetd_config" /usr/lib/systemd/system/bande-greeter.service
test -x "$(sed -n 's/^command = "\([^ "]*\).*/\1/p' "$greetd_config")"
display_manager() {
    grep -qx "$1" /etc/X11/default-display-manager
    [ "$(basename "$(readlink /etc/systemd/system/display-manager.service)")" = "$(basename "$1").service" ]
}
display_manager /usr/bin/bande-greeter
test ! -e /usr/lib/systemd/system/greetd.service.d
grep -q agreety /etc/greetd/config.toml
service=$(sed -n 's/^service = "\(.*\)"/\1/p' "$greetd_config")
grep -q pam_loginuid "$(ls /etc/pam.d/"$service" /usr/lib/pam.d/"$service" 2>/dev/null | head -n 1)"
[ "$(stat -c '%a %U %G' /var/lib/bande-greeter/failed)" = "3733 root _greetd" ]

pictures=/var/lib/bande-greeter/pictures
[ "$(stat -c '%a %U %G' "$pictures")" = "3733 root _greetd" ]
useradd --create-home ada
useradd --create-home alan
runuser -u ada -- sh -c "umask 077; echo picture > $pictures/\$(id -u); chmod 640 $pictures/\$(id -u)"
[ "$(runuser -u _greetd -- cat "$pictures/$(id -u ada)")" = picture ]
refused() {
    if "$@" > /dev/null 2>&1; then
        echo "allowed: $*"
        exit 1
    fi
}
refused runuser -u alan -- cat "$pictures/$(id -u ada)"
refused runuser -u alan -- ls "$pictures"
refused runuser -u alan -- rm -f "$pictures/$(id -u ada)"
test -e "$pictures/$(id -u ada)"
DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive dpkg --purge bande-greeter < /dev/null
display_manager /usr/sbin/greetd
test ! -e "$pictures"
echo "bande-desktop brings a login window and sound"
